5.03. Since the difference is significantly higher than 0, the processor 126 would classify the voxel as intravascular. Dividing the ASI for the medium baseline by the ASI for the high baseline would result in a dividend of 1.17. Since the dividend is greater than about 1 but less than 2, the processor 126 would classify the voxel as containing a vein. Because the extraction fraction of the arterial blood is reduced during hypoxia, the magnetic signal in the vein changes only slightly when the baseline is varied. [0095]  In some embodiments, instead of calculating ASI and basing the determination on a comparison between the first and second ASI, the processor 126 calculates the maximum relaxation rate and bases the determination on a comparison between the first and second maximum relaxation rates. The maximum relaxation rate for a voxel may becalculated according to Equation 2, where TE represents echo time and  SVG
